AWEN 0.1

PROJECT New Project
OUTPUT responsive task-list website
ROOT .

SOURCES
  PRODUCT ./docs/requirements.md AUTHORITATIVE
  UX ./docs/experience.md AUTHORITATIVE
  CONTENT ./docs/welcome.md AUTHORITATIVE VERBATIM
  ENGINEERING ./docs/engineering.md AUTHORITATIVE
  REFERENCE ./docs/notes.md CONTEXT

IMPLEMENTATION
  ROOT ./src/
  TESTS ./tests/

STACK
  HTML
  CSS
  JavaScript

TOOLS
  AGENT capable coding agent
  TEST browser and automated checks

BEHAVIOR
  visitors can add tasks, mark them complete and remove them
  tasks remain after refreshing the page
  an empty task is not accepted
  the welcome text is visible on first load

REQUIRE
  responsive layout and keyboard-accessible controls
  semantic HTML and labelled inputs
  persist tasks in browser local storage
  no account or network service needed

PREFER
  plain JavaScript and minimal dependencies

AVOID
  unnecessary frameworks or build steps

FORBID
  remote transmission of task content
  replacing functional task controls with a static mock

SEAMS
  STORAGE browser local storage is the accepted MVP storage boundary; no server persistence is required

APPROVAL
  HUMAN any external service or authentication feature

NON-GOALS
  collaboration and user accounts
  cloud synchronisation

BLOCKERS
  none

EXECUTION
  1. Read every declared source in order and identify any conflicts before coding.
  2. Implement the welcome view and accessible task form in ./src/.
  3. Implement adding, completing and deleting tasks.
  4. Persist tasks locally and restore them after refresh.
  5. Add tests in ./tests/ for required task behaviour and persistence.
  6. Run the tests and review narrow and wide layouts.
  7. Report results and any unmet acceptance criteria.

DONE WHEN
  1. The exact welcome text from ./docs/welcome.md appears on the page.
  2. A visitor can add, complete and remove tasks using keyboard controls.
  3. Blank tasks are rejected.
  4. Tasks survive a page refresh in the same browser.
  5. No task content is transmitted to an external service.
  6. Relevant tests pass and the layout works at narrow and wide widths.
